Fictional EP Tracklist

Track 1: The Express Brakes Screech Against the Halocline
- Story & Context: Maintenance crew chief Vance stood on the dripping maintenance gantry as the salvage lift groaned, watching a massive bundle of fiber-optic cable snap like a whip in the freezing Atlantic darkness and drag three warning buoys down into the black void. "The iron teeth are chewing through the line again," he muttered into his comm-rig, desperately trying to lock the hydraulic winch before the pressure wave flattened the sub-assembly. This sudden infrastructural failure was the exact moment the crew first heard the low-frequency blues shuffles echoing through the transatlantic lines, birthing the entire Abyssal Shunt movement.
- Visual & Lyrics Prompt: A rusted train locomotive suspended impossibly over a pitch-black underwater trench, its iron wheels locked mid-slide as sparks fly upward into a wall of dark, churning ocean water.

Track 2: Platform 9 Sinks Beneath the Mud
- Story & Context: Saturation diver Maeve sat alone in the dim amber glow of the decompression habitat, running a trembling thumb over a rusted brass guitar slide while listening to the rhythmic clicking of the station's structural rivets failing under the crushing weight of the continental shelf. "Nobody gets off this bottom-train alive," she whispered to the empty steel chamber, realizing the rescue submersible had missed its final timetable window. Her claustrophobic confession became the haunting vocal sample that anchors this track's sluggish, hypnotic marimba pulse.
- Visual & Lyrics Prompt: An abandoned underground railway platform slowly flooding with murky, silt-laden water, where vintage wooden benches and rusted timetable boards are half-submerged under a heavy, reflective mirror of brine.

Track 3: Timetable for the Drowned Express
- Story & Context: Deep beneath the Grand Banks, the automated shipwreck memorial station continues to broadcast its phantom arrivals on loop, long after the last human divers abandoned the salvage rig. "All inbound souls please mind the gap in reality," chirped the distorted, water-logged public address system as the automated tech-house beat locked into an endless, inescapable groove. This rhythmic myth remains the ultimate anthem of the deep-sea splicers, celebrating the moment they traded surface life for the endless trance of the abyss.
- Visual & Lyrics Prompt: A ghostly, bioluminescent railway clock melting into the sea floor, surrounded by schools of blind deep-sea fish swimming in perfect geometric synchronization through tangled bundles of glowing fiber-optic cables.

